\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \emph  {The Debutantes' Ball:} At the debutantes' ball, young nano-women gather in their finery at the edge of the stage to weep because none of the nano-boys will dance with them. The micrograph shows an array of 50 nm wide posts with a periodicity of 100 nm. The posts consist of PMMA on top of an antireflection coating. The substrate consists of a 250 nm thick layer of silicon nitride on silicon. Winner of the 1995 ``Most Bizarre Micrograph'' prize. Submitted by Tim Savas, Massachusetts Institute of Technology.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
